Fixes for parallel 1.2.15, none of them in a release yet. Drop this file
once a release carries all three.

1. PHP 8.6: HT_PACKED_SIZE became an inline function, so the
   `#ifdef HT_PACKED_SIZE` feature tests turned false and packed arrays
   were walked as Bucket arrays (segfault on any list crossing threads).
   Upstream: https://github.com/krakjoe/parallel/pull/393 (merged).

2. PHP 8.6: zend_closure.this_ptr changed from a zval to a zend_object*.
   parallel mirrors that struct, so a bound closure crossing threads
   corrupted the heap.
   Upstream: https://github.com/krakjoe/parallel/pull/429

3. All versions: a Closure over an internal function (strlen(...)) was
   treated as an op_array and segfaulted. It is now rejected like any
   other illegal value.
   Upstream: https://github.com/krakjoe/parallel/pull/430

With these, upstream's suite is clean on 8.1-8.6 zts, bar three 8.6 tests
whose expected output lacks new deprecation notices (021, 051, 063).

--- a/src/check.c
+++ b/src/check.c
@@ -487,6 +487,11 @@
 
 static zend_always_inline bool php_parallel_check_closure(zend_closure_t *closure)
 { /* {{{ */
+	/* a Closure over an internal function (e.g. strlen(...)) has no op_array */
+	if (closure->func.type != ZEND_USER_FUNCTION) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	return php_parallel_check_statics(&closure->func, NULL, NULL) &&
 	       php_parallel_check_function(&closure->func, NULL, NULL);
 } /* }}} */
